INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'card_grid', 'tour', '{}'::jsonb, ARRAY['package:bali-bromo-ijen-3d2n','package:bali-ijen-bromo-madakaripura-3d2n','package:bali-ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-4d3n','package:bali-ijen-papuma-tumpak-sewu-bromo-5d4n']::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/tours/from-bali';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 3, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"Bali Landing Page — Website Copy","body_md":"# Bali Landing Page — Website Copy\n\n---\n\n## Hero Section\n\n### H1\nPrivate East Java Volcano Tours from Bali — Police-Led, Ferry Included\n\n### Subheadline\n4 private packages: Kawah Ijen, Mount Bromo, Tumpak Sewu & Papuma Beach. Cross from Bali to East Java with your own vehicle, your own crew, and no hidden costs.\n\n### Credibility Line\nLicensed operator NIB 1102230032918 · Trustpilot 4.8/5 (51 reviews) · Founded 2015\n\n---\n\n## Lead Paragraph\n\nEvery JVTO Bali package is 100% private — your group, your vehicle, your schedule. The Bali–Java ferry crossing (Gilimanuk–Ketapang) is included in every package. Mr. Sam, the founder, is an active officer of the Indonesian Tourist Police (Ditpamobvit East Java): every route, safety decision, and written rule traces back to someone who answers to police protocol. What''s included is written before you book. What it costs is confirmed before you pay.\n\n---\n\n## Route Overview\n\n### Section Heading\nBali to East Java — what the route looks like\n\nAll four Bali packages cross from Bali to East Java by ferry on Day 1. Three packages finish in Surabaya (one-way overland); one package returns you to Bali on Day 3. The route flows east-to-west: Ijen crater first, Bromo last (or Bromo first, Ijen last on the 3D2N return package). Pick-up is from your Bali hotel or address.\n\n---\n\n## Package Section\n\n### Section Heading\n4 Private Tours from Bali\n\nAll packages: dedicated vehicle, English-speaking crew, ferry crossing (Gilimanuk–Ketapang), entrance fees, accommodation + breakfast, gas masks + trekking poles (Ijen), mineral water, JVTO T-shirt. Price per person — no hidden local payments.\n\n---\n\n### 3-Day Packages\n\n**3 Day Bromo & Ijen Volcano Discovery — Returns to Bali**\nThe only Bali-return package. Cross to East Java on Day 1, reach Bromo side for sunrise staging. Day 2: Bromo crater sunrise (private 4WD Jeep included), Madakaripura Waterfall canyon, transfer to Bondowoso for Ijen staging. Day 3: Ijen night hike, descent, and ferry return to Bali.\n\n*Day-by-day:*\n| Day | Summary | Hotel |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Bali → ferry → Bromo side | Joglo Kecombrang Bromo |\n| 2 | Bromo sunrise · Madakaripura · transfer to Bondowoso | Riverside Homestay |\n| 3 | Ijen climb · descent · return ferry → Bali | — |\n\n*From IDR 4,050,000/person (2 pax) · IDR 2,850,000/person (11+ pax)*\n\n---\n\n**3 Day Ijen, Bromo & Madakaripura — Bali to Surabaya**\nIjen first, Bromo second. Cross to Banyuwangi on Day 1 for Ijen staging. Day 2: Ijen night hike, transfer west to Bromo side. Day 3: Bromo crater sunrise, Madakaripura Waterfall, finish in Surabaya. Solo pricing available.\n\nBlue Fire is a natural phenomenon subject to weather and gas activity. Gas masks provided by JVTO. A health certificate is mandatory for every guest before Kawah Ijen crater entry, per BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024; JVTO coordinates clinic workflow for every guest under BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024.\n\n*Day-by-day:*\n| Day | Summary | Hotel |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Bali → ferry → Banyuwangi for Ijen staging | Luminor Hotel |\n| 2 | Ijen climb · descent · transfer to Bromo side | Joglo Kecombrang Bromo |\n| 3 | Bromo sunrise · Madakaripura · finish in Surabaya | — |\n\n*From IDR 7,500,000/person (solo) · IDR 4,050,000/person (2 pax) · IDR 2,850,000/person (11+ pax)*\n\n---\n\n### 4-Day Package\n\n**4 Day Ijen, Papuma Beach, Tumpak Sewu & Bromo Expedition — Bali to Surabaya**\nFour destinations across four days. Cross to Banyuwangi on Day 1 for Ijen staging. Day 2: Ijen crater, transfer to Papuma Beach coastal area (Jember). Day 3: Tumpak Sewu curtain waterfall (~120 m), transfer to Bromo side. Day 4: Bromo crater sunrise, finish in Surabaya. Solo pricing available.\n\n*Day-by-day:*\n| Day | Summary | Hotel |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Bali → ferry → Banyuwangi for Ijen staging | Luminor Hotel |\n| 2 | Ijen climb · descent · transfer to Papuma | Doho Homestay |\n| 3 | Tumpak Sewu · transfer to Bromo side | Joglo Kecombrang Bromo |\n| 4 | Bromo sunrise · finish in Surabaya | — |\n\n*From IDR 9,050,000/person (solo) · IDR 4,900,000/person (2 pax) · IDR 3,475,000/person (11+ pax)*\n\n---\n\n### 5-Day Package\n\n**5 Day Ijen, Papuma Beach, Tumpak Sewu & Bromo Discovery — Bali to Surabaya**\nExtended version of the 4D3N circuit with additional time built into each transfer segment. Recommended for groups who prefer a less compressed pace. Cross to Banyuwangi on Day 1; finish in Surabaya on Day 5.\n\n*Day-by-day:*\n| Day | Summary | Hotel |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Bali → ferry → Banyuwangi for Ijen staging | Luminor Hotel |\n| 2 | Ijen climb · descent · transfer to Papuma side | Doho Homestay |\n| 3 | Papuma area · transfer to Tumpak Sewu staging | Joglo Kecombrang Bromo |\n| 4 | Tumpak Sewu · transfer toward Bromo | Joglo Kecombrang Bromo |\n| 5 | Bromo sunrise · finish in Surabaya | — |\n\n*From IDR 5,450,000/person (2 pax) · IDR 4,050,000/person (11+ pax)*\n\n---\n\n## What''s Included Section\n\n### Section Heading\nEvery Bali package includes — in writing\n\n- **Bali–Java ferry crossing**: Gilimanuk–Ketapang, both directions (3D2N Bali-return package) or one-way Bali-to-Java (all other packages).\n- **Private transport**: AC MPV (1–3 guests) or Toyota Hiace (4–9 guests). Fuel, tolls, and parking included.\n- **Dedicated crew**: English-speaking driver-guide (1–3 guests), or professional driver + escort guide (4+ guests). Licensed local site guides at key locations.\n- **Entrance fees and permits** to all attractions on the itinerary.\n- **Accommodation + breakfast** (all nights, per itinerary).\n- **Private 4WD Jeep** for Bromo crater area. One jeep per ≤4 guests; additional jeeps arranged for larger groups.\n- **Gas masks and trekking poles** for Ijen crater hike.\n- **Health-certificate screening coordination** for Ijen routes for every guest under BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024.\n- **Daily mineral water supply**.\n- **Full pick-up to drop-off assistance** from your Bali hotel or address.\n- **JVTO travel T-shirt** (1 per participant).\n\n**Not included**: flights, tips, personal expenses, travel insurance, Indonesian VISA (if applicable).\n\n**End point note**: Three of four Bali packages finish in Surabaya — plan onward transport from Surabaya (flights, train, or bus) in advance.\n\n---\n\n## Why JVTO Section\n\n### Section Heading\nThe facts behind the booking\n\n**Police-Led Operations**\nMr. Sam holds the rank of Bripka and serves as an active officer of Ditpamobvit East Java (Tourist Police). Independent national press — Detik.com, 2021-03-14 — confirms active-duty status. No other tour operator in East Java is led by a serving Tourist Police officer.\n\n**100% Private — No Shared Groups**\nYour booking receives a dedicated vehicle and crew. No join-in option exists. Group size determines vehicle type (MPV or Hiace); timing and route decisions apply to your group only.\n\n**All-Inclusive — Written Before You Book**\nInclusions and exclusions are published on every package page and confirmed in your voucher. Ferry crossing, entrance fees, accommodation, gas masks, and all transport costs are bundled. Mid-trip negotiations over ticket costs, fuel, or meals do not occur on JVTO routes.\n\n**Verifiable Credentials**\nNIB 1102230032918 is verifiable via the Indonesian OSS system. HPWKI membership is registered under AHU-0001072.AH.01.07.TAHUN 2024. BBKSDA clearance and POLPAR authorisation are on file. All guides hold KTA credentials (2024 issuance). Dr. Ahmad Irwandanu holds a valid SIP license (Kemenkes/KKI verifiable).\n\n---\n\n## Trust Signals Section\n\n### Section Heading\nCheck us before you book\n\n| Signal | Source |\n|---|---|\n| Trustpilot: 4.8/5 · 51 reviews | Independent (verified 2026-05-09) |\n| Google Maps: 4.90/5 · 123 reviews | Independent |\n| TripAdvisor: 4.95/5 · 21 reviews | Independent |\n| NIB 1102230032918 | OSS-verifiable |\n| Founder: active Tourist Police officer | Detik.com press record, 2021 |\n| ISIC Student Tours | Provider ID 259268 (isic.org verifiable) |\n| Founded: 2015 | Booking.com 2015 award, Stefan Loose 2016 p. 287 |\n\nJVTO does not ask for CVV codes, OTP codes, or online banking passwords via chat or email. Pay only via the official JVTO website, listed bank accounts, or confirmed WhatsApp +62 822 4478 8833.\n\n---\n\n## Booking Section\n\n### Section Heading\nBook direct — no agency fees\n\n1. **WhatsApp** +62 822 4478 8833 with your dates, group size, preferred package, and Bali pick-up location.\n2. Receive a price confirmation (per the pricing table for your group size).\n3. Pay a 20% deposit via Xendit secure checkout (card or QRIS) to confirm the booking; if Day 1 is within 14 days, up to 100% may be required.\n4. Receive your e-voucher with full trip details and a pre-trip guide.\n\n**Deposit**: 20% of total (up to 100% if Day 1 is within 14 days), via Xendit secure checkout — card or QRIS. Wise or bank transfer for the balance.\n**Balance deadline**: card — 5 days before Day 1 · bank wire/Wise — 3 days before Day 1.\n**Cancellation ≥ 48h before Day 1**: 100% converted to Lifetime Package Credit (no expiry, transferable).\n**Cancellation < 48h before Day 1**: forfeited. No Package Credit.\n\n**Student pricing available** for verified ISIC cardholders (Provider ID 259268). Ask at booking.\n\n**Group incentive (direct bookings only)**: 18 paying guests → 1 free place · 35 paying → 2 free places · 50 paying → 3 free places + 5% group discount.\n\n---\n\n*Sources: [[products/packages-overview]] · [[products/packages-full-pricing]] · [[products/packages-itineraries]] · [[website/copy-bank]] · [[website/brand-voice]] · [[website/aeo-claims]] · [[credentials/trust-signals]] · [[credentials/legal-licenses]] · [[people/agung-sambuko]] · [[sources/ssot-v6]]*","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/tours/from-bali';
