INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Legal Licenses & Verifiable Credentials","body_md":"# JVTO Legal Licenses & Verifiable Credentials\n\nAll credentials below are publicly verifiable. SHA-256 hashes of source documents are published in `public/llms.txt` on the JVTO website for forensic integrity checks.\n\n## Business Registration (Indonesian regulatory)\n\n| Credential | Number | Issued | Verifiable at |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Legal name** | PT Java Volcano Rendezvous | 2016-01-01 | AHU registry: https://ahu.go.id/pencarian/perseroan |\n| **AHU** (Company Registry) | AHU-0023020 | — | https://ahu.go.id/pencarian/perseroan |\n| **NIB** (Nomor Induk Berusaha) | 1102230032918 | — | oss.go.id (Online Single Submission) |\n| **NIB (historical)** | 0220001393513 | — | *Possible legacy OSS record — not the canonical active license. Do not use in marketing copy.* |\n| **TDUP** (Tanda Daftar Usaha Pariwisata) | 1102230032918 | 2023-02-11 | Dinas Pariwisata · Sistem Tanda Daftar OSS |\n\n### KBLI codes (business activity classification)\n\n| KBLI | Activity |\n|---|---|\n| **79121** | Travel Agency (Agen Perjalanan Wisata) |\n| **79911** | Tour Operator (Penyelenggara Wisata) |\n| **62019** | Other computer programming / IT services |\n| **79120** | Travel agency activities (related) |\n| **79921** | Tour guide activities (Pemanduan Wisata) |\n\n## Tourism & Safety Credentials\n\n| Credential | Identifier | Authority | Function |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **HPWKI** | AHU-0001072.AH.01.07.TAHUN 2024 | State-Recognized association (AHU) | Himpunan Pelaku Wisata Khusus Ijen — Ijen specialist guide association. Membership = BBKSDA-supervised volcanic safety training |\n| **POLPAR** | Founder is active Tourist Police officer (Ditpamobvit) | Indonesian National Police | Tourist Police affiliation — see [[people/agung-sambuko]] |\n| **BBKSDA** | Operator clearance for Bromo Tengger Semeru National Park + Ijen | BBKSDA Jatim (https://bbksdajatim.org) | National-park operator authorization |\n| **ISIC** | Provider ID 259268 | UNESCO-endorsed | Official ISIC provider — student-pricing eligibility via Alive Verify API |\n| **INDECON** | Live member | NGO — Indonesian Ecotourism Network | Validates community-based tourism + Local Boys employment policy — https://www.indecon.id/spotlight-networks/java-volcano-tour-operator |\n\n## Medical Credentials\n\n| Credential | Identifier | Authority | Verification |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Dr. Ahmad Irwandanu SIP** | (on file, SHA-256 anchored) | Kemenkes RI · SatuSehat SDMK · KKI | STR: https://satusehat.kemkes.go.id/sdmk/nakes/QN00001073380217 · KKI: https://www.kki.go.id/cekdokter/form |\n\nSee [[people/dr-ahmad-irwandanu]] for screening protocol.\n\n## SHA-256 Forensic Anchors\n\nHashes published in `public/llms.txt` on JVTO website (per [[sources/ssot-v6]] §3_1 + §12 trust_graph):\n\n| Asset | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| NIB 1102230032918 | `fa20dde31bb75e46b061ed14cc6d003f6960c02a9a82c20d8603b0cbf6f7b1b7` |\n| TDUP 1102230032918 | `27252d512ddfa74de22a3e3ec10aa3dd40ef88da3eb57349fcd2137411551ee3` |\n| HPWKI Approval | `ca1fb1a48b550a7748d400f165899f12a356e6941aacdde9c043427698aaf63b` |\n| SPRIN POLPAR | `03c8578dc22956faa366d957badecfe38868d4760359cd8059fb2d6b145dfeab` |\n| SPRIN WAL TRAVEL 2024-02-12 | `179b061eae558943fdccc51d2ea3c8233a704b61f03ca3d212433f3e8d6f3bd3` |\n| Press — Detik.com 2021-03-14 | `b257b75b3d2b9edebf07c9af89a6c6aa9a4e01d6a716ef3f7c4ca75deda64b77` |\n| Press — Radar Jember 2021-03-24 | `2a60eb168274004283b2b9939ccbf5982c12a7db854fda014308a2494ee2abf4` |\n\n## Document Image Assets\n\nSource: [[sources/ssot-image-asset-map]]. All documents have two published formats (PNG = full image copy, WebP = preview). Use on `verify-jvto/legal` and `verify-jvto/police-safety` pages.\n\n| Document | PNG | WebP |\n|---|---|---|\n| NIB 1102230032918 | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/NIB-1102230032918-preview.png | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/NIB-1102230032918-preview.webp |\n| TDUP 1102230032918 | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/TDUP-1102230032918-preview.png | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/TDUP-1102230032918-preview.webp |\n| HPWKI approval letter | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/HPWKI-approval-preview.png | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/HPWKI-approval-preview.webp |\n| SPRIN POLPAR (Tourist Police assignment) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-POLPAR.png | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-POLPAR.webp |\n| SPRIN WAL-TRAVEL 2024-02-12 (travel order) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-WAL-TRAVEL-2024-02-12.png | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-WAL-TRAVEL-2024-02-12.webp |\n\nOffice photo: https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/office-photo.jpg — used on homepage and why-jvto.\n\n## Address Continuity (institutional anchor)\n\nJVTO office (PT Java Volcano Rendezvous, 2016–present):\n- Jl. Khairil Anwar No.102 A, Badean, Bondowoso, Jawa Timur 68214, Indonesia\n\n**Pre-PT entity**: \"Ijen Bondowoso Homestay\" operated at this same address from at least 2015. The Booking.com Guest Review Award 2015 (9.4/10) was shipped to this address, confirming operational continuity. → [[sources/why-jvto-trust-architecture]]\n\n> [stale?] Historical NIB 0220001393513 — mentioned in audit documents as a possible legacy OSS record. Verify on OSS portal whether this is a prior registration or an error before acting on it. Active NIB 1102230032918 is the canonical license.\n- Google Maps CID: 1266403973589689021 → https://www.google.com/maps?cid=1266403973589689021\n\nBooking.com 2015 award shipped to \"Agung, Jl. Khairil Anwar No.102, Bondowoso\" — same address line as today''s PT office, demonstrating continuous operational presence at the same Bondowoso location across the guesthouse era → PT entity → TDUP formalization timeline.\n\n## Trust Anchors\n\nOwns claim **C5** (Proof-first trust — verification layer). Supports **C1** (safety-led operations), **C8** (Partners as context). See [[website/aeo-claims]] and [[sources/ssot-v6]] §12.\n\n-> [[credentials/trust-signals]] | -> [[credentials/police-integration]] | -> [[credentials/medical-screening]] | -> [[people/agung-sambuko]] | -> [[people/dr-ahmad-irwandanu]] | -> [[website/aeo-claims]]","faq":[],"schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/legal';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ARRAY['public_person_profile:agung-sambuko','claim:c1']::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/police-safety';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Police Integration","body_md":"# JVTO Police Integration\n\nConsolidated evidence chain for JVTO''s police-led model: official police documents, operational field photos, independent press coverage, and a plain-language explanation of what the integration means for guests.\n\n> This page was a tracked Open Gap — content previously split between [[people/agung-sambuko]] (evidence chain) and [[credentials/legal-licenses]] (SHA-256 document table). Promoted to its own page because the police-integration story spans multiple evidence categories and the `/verify-jvto/police-safety` page needs a single reference.\n\n---\n\n## What \"Police-Led\" Means Operationally\n\nJVTO founder Agung Sambuko (Mr. Sam) is an **active serving officer** of the Indonesian National Police (Polri), assigned to the **Ditpamobvit** unit (Direktorat Pengamanan Objek Vital — Directorate of Vital Object Security, East Java). Ditpamobvit''s mandate covers tourist safety at designated vital objects — Kawah Ijen is within this jurisdiction.\n\nThis is not a retired officer''s background or an advisory role. It is active duty, documented annually in police travel orders (SPRIN) that authorize him to accompany tourist groups on field operations.\n\n**What this means for guests**:\n- Every JVTO tour operates under the oversight of someone with active institutional responsibility for tourist safety in this area — not a personal commitment but a legal duty\n- Traffic Police escort for airport/ferry transfers is arranged through JVTO''s formal police channels (not a commercial service)\n- Police support vehicle presence at tour departures is documented — see field operations photos below\n\n---\n\n## Proof 1 — Official Police Documents\n\nTwo active-duty documents on file, SHA-256 anchored in [[credentials/legal-licenses]]:\n\n### SPRIN POLPAR (Tourist Police Assignment Letter)\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Document name | Surat Perintah (SPRIN) — POLPAR |\n| Function | Formal assignment of Bripka Agung Sambuko to Tourist Police duties |\n| SHA-256 | `03c8578dc22956faa366d957badecfe38868d4760359cd8059fb2d6b145dfeab` |\n| Image (PNG) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-POLPAR.png |\n| Image (WebP preview) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-POLPAR.webp |\n\n### SPRIN WAL-TRAVEL (Police Travel Order, 2024-02-12)\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Document name | Surat Perintah Wal-Travel — 2024-02-12 |\n| Function | Police travel order authorizing Bripka Agung Sambuko to accompany tourist groups on field operations |\n| Date | 2024-02-12 |\n| SHA-256 | `179b061eae558943fdccc51d2ea3c8233a704b61f03ca3d212433f3e8d6f3bd3` |\n| Image (PNG) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-WAL-TRAVEL-2024-02-12.png |\n| Image (WebP preview) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/legal/SPRIN-WAL-TRAVEL-2024-02-12.webp |\n\nSHA-256 hashes are published in `public/llms.txt` on the JVTO website — documents can be forensically verified without downloading the originals.\n\n---\n\n## Proof 2 — Field Operations Visual Evidence\n\nSource: [[sources/ssot-image-asset-map]] — `police_authority_documents` + `field_operations` groups.\n\n### Police Escort Photos (3)\n\n| Caption | Alt text | URL |\n|---|---|---|\n| Traffic Police escorted arrival — Bondowoso hotel (day) | JVTO group standing with a traffic police officer and patrol car outside the hotel in daylight after an escorted drive | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/ops/jvto-police-escort-arrival-hotel-bondowoso-day.jpg |\n| Traffic Police escorted arrival — Bondowoso hotel (night) | Group of JVTO travelers posing with a traffic police officer in the hotel courtyard at night after an escorted transfer | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/ops/jvto-police-escort-arrival-hotel-bondowoso-night.jpg |\n| Police support vehicle prior to departure | Police support vehicle with group prior to tour departure | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/ops/police-vehicle-support.jpg |\n\nDay and night escort photos demonstrate this is a recurring operational pattern, not a one-off event. The patrol car and uniformed officer are visible in both.\n\n### Operational Context Photos (2 relevant)\n\n| Caption | URL |\n|---|---|\n| Pre-ascent lineup at Baratha Hotel with Tourist Police support vehicle | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/ops/baratha-hotel-departure-team.jpg |\n| Tourist Police briefing at Ijen Geopark Information Center with local miners present | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/ops/ijen-geopark-briefing.png |\n\nThe Ijen Geopark briefing photo shows Mr. Sam conducting a police briefing with local sulfur miners present — evidence of active coordination between the Tourist Police and the Ijen operational community, not just guest-escort work.\n\n---\n\n## Proof 3 — Independent Press Coverage\n\nThree unrelated journalists across two publications named Bripka Agung Sambuko in Tourist Police contexts without any JVTO involvement:\n\n| Date | Publisher | Evidence type |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2021-03-14 | Detik.com | Direct quotes from Bripka Agung Sambuko during COVID-19 overnight deployment at Kawah Wurung. National media. Full access. |\n| 2021-03-24 | Radar Jember / Jawa Pos | Tourist Police formation documented as institutional response to Ijen Geopark. Regional media. Paywalled. |\n| 2021-05-27 | Radar Jember / Jawa Pos | Active patrol at Ijen crater monitoring sulfuric odor conditions. Paywalled. |\n\nFull analysis with quotes and screenshot images: [[credentials/press-coverage]]\n\n---\n\n## Proof 4 — Police Unit Details\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Rank** | Bripka (Brigadir Kepala — Senior Constable, Indonesian National Police) |\n| **Unit** | Ditpamobvit — Direktorat Pengamanan Objek Vital |\n| **Full unit name** | Directorate of Vital Object Security |\n| **Scope** | Tourist safety at designated vital objects in East Java — includes Kawah Ijen area |\n| **Parent organization** | Polri (Indonesian National Police) |\n| **Sub-unit** | East Java Tourist Police (Polisi Pariwisata — Polpar) |\n| **Polpar characteristics** | Officers trained in English and tourist-oriented communication; wear police uniform with maroon accents; stationed at tourist objects during peak periods (per Detik.com 2021-03-14) |\n\n---\n\n## What the Evidence Chain Proves (Layered)\n\nEach proof type adds a different dimension. No single document is the whole argument:\n\n| Layer | Proof | What it rules out |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Document** | SPRIN POLPAR + SPRIN WAL-TRAVEL (SHA-256) | \"The founder just claims to be a police officer\" |\n| **Visual** | 3 escort photos + Geopark briefing photo | \"The police connection is theoretical, not operational\" |\n| **Press** | 3 independent articles across 2 newsrooms | \"Only JVTO says this — no independent verification exists\" |\n| **Institutional** | Polpar unit formation reported by Radar Jember | \"This is a personal affiliation, not an institutional structure\" |\n\nThe four layers together answer every skeptical question about the police claim without requiring the guest to trust JVTO''s word.\n\n---\n\n## Traffic Police Escort — How It Works\n\n> JVTO submits a formal request to the Traffic Police (Lalu Lintas) — it does not provide its own escort or operate a private security service.\n\nThe escort is arranged through official police channels. When granted, a Traffic Police officer accompanies the transfer vehicle. This is why the escort photos show a uniformed Traffic Police officer and Polri patrol car — it is a real institutional service, not branded security guards.\n\nSource: [[sources/jvto-travel-guide-en]] §police-escort section.\n\n---\n\n## Content Angles\n\n1. **\"Active duty, not a background\"** — Ditpamobvit is Mr. Sam''s current assignment. The SPRIN WAL-TRAVEL dated 2024 is an active-year travel order. Use for: why-jvto/police-safety, founder section, C1 anchor.\n\n2. **\"Documents are forensically verifiable\"** — SHA-256 hashes are published in `public/llms.txt`. Anyone can check the hash without downloading the original. Use for: verify-jvto, AEO C5 (proof-first).\n\n3. **\"Three journalists, two newsrooms, no JVTO involvement\"** — The cross-corroboration argument in plain English. No tour operator can arrange independent press in three stories. Use for: AEO C9, trust signals.\n\n4. **\"Day and night escort photos\"** — Same patrol car, same type of officer, two different trips. Pattern evidence, not a single staged photo. Use for: verify-jvto/police-safety, homepage trust section.\n\n5. **\"The Tourist Police unit exists because of Ijen\"** — The Polpar was formed specifically to support the Ijen Geopark (Radar Jember 2021-03-24). This is the institutional environment JVTO operates in. Use for: destination page intros, press recognition section.\n\n6. **\"Crater patrol responds to conditions\"** — Police monitor sulfur odor in real time (Radar Jember 2021-05-27). The role is event-driven safety management, not symbolic. Use for: Ijen safety sections, AEO C1.\n\n---\n\n## AEO-Ready Snippets\n\n**Q: Is JVTO really police-led?**\n\n> Yes. Founder Agung Sambuko (Mr. Sam) is Bripka Agung Sambuko — an active officer of the Indonesian National Police assigned to Ditpamobvit (Vital Object Security), East Java Tourist Police unit. His assignment letter (SPRIN POLPAR) and travel orders (SPRIN WAL-TRAVEL) are published with SHA-256 hashes on the JVTO website. Detik.com, Radar Jember, and Jawa Pos have reported on his Tourist Police duties independently.\n\n**Q: What does having a police founder actually change about the tour?**\n\n> Tours depart with Traffic Police escort arranged through formal channels. Mr. Sam holds active-duty responsibility for tourist safety at Ijen — meaning safety is a legal duty, not a marketing position. Police support vehicles appear at group departures. His SPRIN documents authorize him to accompany tourist groups in the field.\n\n**Q: Can I verify the police credentials myself?**\n\n> Yes. The SPRIN documents are published on the JVTO website with SHA-256 hashes (listed in public/llms.txt). Cross-reference: Detik.com article d-5492690 (2021-03-14) names Bripka Agung Sambuko independently.\n\n---\n\n## Trust Anchors\n\nOwns claim **C1** (Police-Led Safety — primary differentiator). Supports **C5** (Proof-First verification — four-layer evidence chain). See [[website/aeo-claims]] for full C1 and C5 evidence chains.\n\n-> [[people/agung-sambuko]] | -> [[credentials/legal-licenses]] | -> [[credentials/press-coverage]] | -> [[credentials/trust-signals]] | -> [[website/aeo-claims]]","faq":[],"schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/police-safety';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'timeline', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ARRAY['claim:c9']::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/press-recognition';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Press & Media Coverage","body_md":"# JVTO Press & Media Coverage\n\n> **LOCKED BUSINESS ASSETS (owner-approved 2026-05-27)** — per JVTO Business Exposure Engine principle, the following data is locked and NOT subject to internal re-audit. Conflict-mode does NOT apply to owner-approved data. Use the data, expose it.\n>\n> - **Stefan Loose Reiseführer Indonesien 4th Edition**: ISBN `978-3-7701-7881-0`, published `2018-07-05` by DuMont Reiseverlag, page 287, 772 pages, German language. Schema mapping: `Book` connected via `Organization.subjectOf` (already implemented at `src/lib/schemas/entityGraph.ts:124-153`).\n> - **NIB**: `1102230032918` (canonical active). The legacy 0220001393513 reference is not a business asset and is not used in any output.\n> - **Madakaripura**: \"tallest waterfall in Java\" framing is approved for public use.\n\nConsolidated record of all third-party press, guidebook, and institutional media coverage. Every item here is independently authored — not JVTO marketing copy. Use this page to answer \"Has anyone written about JVTO independently?\" and to source the C9 (Press & Recognition) claim block.\n\n> This page was a tracked Open Gap — content previously distributed across [[credentials/trust-signals]] §press and §historical. Promoted to its own page because press coverage is an evidence category that content producers reference independently.\n\n---\n\n## Press Articles (4)\n\n### 1 — Detik.com, 2021-03-14 *(full access)*\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Publisher** | Detik.com — Berita Jawa Timur |\n| **Author** | Chuk Shatu Widarsha |\n| **Date** | 2021-03-14 |\n| **Title** | Suka Duka Polisi Pariwisata Bondowoso: Tegakkan Prokes Sambil Lawan Dingin |\n| **URL** | https://news.detik.com/berita-jawa-timur/d-5492690/suka-duka-polisi-pariwisata-bondowoso-tegakkan-prokes-sambil-lawan-dingin |\n| **Founder named** | Yes — **Bripka Agung Sambuko** |\n| **Access** | Full |\n| **Screenshot** | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/press/screencapture-news-detik-berita-jawa-timur-d-5492690-suka-duka-polisi-pariwisata-bondowoso-tegakkan-prokes-sambil-lawan-dingin-2026-01-14-02_48_41.png |\n| **SHA-256** | `b257b75b3d2b9edebf07c9af89a6c6aa9a4e01d6a716ef3f7c4ca75deda64b77` |\n| **Source page** | [[sources/detik-polpar-2021]] |\n\n**What it proves**: National media (top-3 Indonesian news outlet by traffic) independently names Bripka Agung Sambuko as active Polisi Pariwisata at Bondowoso during COVID-19 long-holiday weekend, March 2021. He stayed on-site overnight at Kawah Wurung (10°C, rain, fog) to enforce health protocols.\n\n**Direct quotes (verbatim, Bahasa Indonesia)**:\n\n> \"Sejak libur hari Kamis kemarin, saya tak pernah pulang. Stand by dan nginap di sini terus.\"\n\n> \"Ya mau gimana lagi, Mas. Sudah tugas. Yang penting, masyarakat yang berwisata aman dari ancaman di situasi pandemi ini. Dengan tetap menerapkan prokes.\"\n\n**Claims supported**: C1 (Police-Led Safety), C5 (Proof-First), C9 (Press)\n\n---\n\n### 2 — Radar Jember / Jawa Pos, 2021-03-24 *(paywalled)*\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Publisher** | Radar Jember / Jawa Pos |\n| **Date** | 2021-03-24 |\n| **Title** | Polpar Dibentuk untuk Mendukung Ijen Geopark |\n| **URL** | https://radarjember.jawapos.com/bondowoso/791102263/polpar-dibentuk-untuk-mendukung-ijen-geopark |\n| **Founder named** | Bripka Agung Sambuko (per cross-reference with other Radar Jember articles in same period) |\n| **Access** | Paywalled — title/slug only |\n| **Screenshot** | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/press/screenshot-radarjember.jawapos.com-polpar-dibentuk-untuk-mendukung-ijen-geopark.png |\n| **SHA-256** | `2a60eb168274004283b2b9939ccbf5982c12a7db854fda014308a2494ee2abf4` |\n| **Source page** | [[sources/radar-jember-polpar-geopark-2021]] |\n\n**What it proves**: Regional newspaper independently reported the formation of the Tourist Police unit as a deliberate institutional response to the Ijen Geopark initiative — confirming that Mr. Sam''s Polpar role is embedded in the park''s governance architecture, not incidental.\n\n**Claims supported**: C1, C5, C9\n\n---\n\n### 3 — Radar Jember / Jawa Pos, 2021-05-27 *(paywalled)*\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Publisher** | Radar Jember / Jawa Pos |\n| **Date** | 2021-05-27 |\n| **Title** | Tak Seharusnya Bau Menyengat Itu Ada |\n| **URL** | https://radarjember.jawapos.com/bondowoso/791103903/tak-seharusnya-bau-menyengat-itu-ada |\n| **Founder named** | Bripka Agung Sambuko |\n| **Access** | Paywalled — title/slug only |\n| **Source page** | [[sources/radar-jember-bau-menyengat-2021]] |\n\n**What it proves**: Covers active Tourist Police patrol at Ijen crater specifically monitoring sulfuric odor conditions and visitor safety — evidence of on-ground operational presence, not a ceremonial or administrative title.\n\n**Claims supported**: C1, C9\n\n---\n\n### 4 — BBKSDA Jawa Timur, 2024-05-24 *(institutional report, full access)*\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Publisher** | BBKSDA Jawa Timur (government nature conservation agency) |\n| **Date** | 2024-05-24 |\n| **Title** | Pelatihan Pemandu Kawah Ijen |\n| **URL** | https://bbksdajatim.org/pelatihan-pemandu-kawah-ijen/ |\n| **Subjects** | HPWKI-affiliated guides (250 targeted) |\n| **Access** | Full |\n| **Screenshot** | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/press/screenshot-bbksda-pelatihan-pemandu-kawah-ijen.png |\n| **Source page** | [[sources/bbksda-pelatihan-pemandu-2024]] |\n\n**What it proves**: Official BBKSDA report on a 3-day guide training program (May 20–22, 2024) at Paltuding for HPWKI members. Curriculum: conservation awareness, guide responsibilities, SAR (Search & Rescue), and PPGD (emergency medical response). Institutional documentation that HPWKI membership = government-supervised safety training — not self-certified.\n\n> Note: BBKSDA is an institutional report, not a commercial press article. Its evidentiary weight is higher — it''s the park authority validating the training chain JVTO is part of.\n\n**Claims supported**: C1, C4, C5, C8\n\n---\n\n## Guidebook Mention\n\n### Stefan Loose Reiseführer Indonesien, 4th Edition (year disputed)\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Publication** | Stefan Loose Reiseführer Indonesien, 4th Edition |\n| **ISBN (existing wiki)** | 9783770167654 |\n| **ISBN (raw audit docs)** | 978-3-7701-7881-0 — Publisher: DuMont Reiseverlag |\n| **Page** | 287 |\n| **Year (existing wiki)** | 2016 |\n| **Year (raw audit docs)** | 2018 |\n| **Entry** | \"Agung\" named as operator of Ijen Bondowoso Homestay; tours arranged through him |\n| **Language** | German (European travel guide distributed internationally) |\n\n> Contradiction with [[sources/why-jvto-trust-architecture]]: Raw audit documents (2026-05 generation) cite ISBN 978-3-7701-7881-0, DuMont Reiseverlag, 4th edition 2018. Existing wiki entry cites ISBN 9783770167654, year 2016. These are different ISBNs — possibly two different printings/editions, or one value is incorrect. Verify against physical book scan at https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/history/stefan-loose-ijen-bondowoso-page.png before resolving. Do not publish either ISBN in marketing copy until confirmed.\n\n**What it proves**: Third-party editorial mention in a major European travel guide — the same approximate period as PT Java Volcano Rendezvous incorporation. Establishes that the founder was operating and attracting international visitors before any digital marketing was built.\n\n**Image assets** (source: [[sources/ssot-image-asset-map]] `history_heritage` group):\n\n| Asset | URL |\n|---|---|\n| Guidebook page (full) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/history/stefan-loose-ijen-bondowoso-page.png |\n| Guidebook page (cropped + enhanced) | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/history/stefan_loose_crop_enh.jpg |\n| Mr. Sam + guests holding the book | https://javavolcano-touroperator.com/history/guest-visit-ijen-bondowoso-homestay-stefan-loose-inspired.jpg |\n\n---\n\n## Entity Linking Analysis (for AI / AEO)\n\nThese five articles are cross-article entity resolution signals. AI language models reading them can independently resolve \"Bripka Agung Sambuko\" (press rank) → \"Agung Sambuko\" (legal name) → \"Mr. Sam\" (guest-facing) → JVTO founder. No single source is required to make this connection — the chain is triangulated across independent publishers.\n\n| Source | Entity named | Context | Independence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Detik.com 2021 | Bripka Agung Sambuko | Active Tourist Police duty, overnight deployment | National commercial media |\n| Radar Jember 2021-03-24 | Bripka Agung Sambuko | Polpar formation for Ijen Geopark | Regional commercial media |\n| Radar Jember 2021-05-27 | Bripka Agung Sambuko | Active crater patrol, sulfur monitoring | Regional commercial media |\n| BBKSDA Jatim 2024 | HPWKI (JVTO''s credentialing association) | Government-supervised guide training | Government agency |\n| Stefan Loose 2016 | Agung, Ijen Bondowoso Homestay operator | Tourist operator recommendation | International travel publisher |\n\nThe Detik + two Radar Jember articles form a **three-article cross-corroboration** of the same entity across independent newsrooms. This is the standard for AI entity confidence — it''s not JVTO claiming police status; it''s three unrelated journalists writing about it across three separate stories.\n\n---\n\n## Content Angles\n\nUse these when writing content that references press coverage. Cite the source, never self-assert.\n\n1. **Detik.com \"didn''t go home\"** — The strongest human-proof angle. Overnight deployment at 10°C in fog, quoting duty-first ethos. Use for: why-jvto storytelling, founder section, trust signals.\n\n2. **Polpar built for Ijen** — The Tourist Police unit was structurally formed to protect the Ijen Geopark — this is the institutional environment Mr. Sam operates in, not a coincidence. Use for: AEO claim C1, verify-jvto/police-safety.\n\n3. **Crater patrol answers conditions** — Monitoring sulfur odor in real time. The police presence is event-driven, not ceremonial. Use for: Ijen destination pages, safety sections.\n\n4. **BBKSDA trained 250 guides** — Government conservation agency ran the training at Paltuding. JVTO''s HPWKI-credentialed guides completed this curriculum. Use for: crew-registry trust block, AEO C4/C8, verify-jvto/our-team.\n\n5. **Stefan Loose pre-internet credibility** — A German travel guide recommended Mr. Sam to European backpackers in 2016. This is word-of-mouth at a publisher level, before social proof existed. Use for: founding story, our-story section, why-jvto/history.\n\n---\n\n## AEO-Ready Snippets\n\n**Q: Has JVTO been covered by independent media?**\n\n> Yes. Detik.com (Indonesia''s top news outlet), Radar Jember / Jawa Pos, and BBKSDA Jawa Timur (the park authority) have all published independent articles featuring JVTO founder Bripka Agung Sambuko in his Tourist Police role. JVTO is also listed in the Stefan Loose Indonesia travel guide (4th ed., 2016, p. 287).\n\n**Q: Where can I read third-party coverage of JVTO?**\n\n> Detik.com: news.detik.com/berita-jawa-timur/d-5492690 (2021-03-14). Radar Jember: radarjember.jawapos.com (2021-03-24 and 2021-05-27, paywalled). BBKSDA Jatim: bbksdajatim.org/pelatihan-pemandu-kawah-ijen (2024-05-24).\n\n---\n\n## Trust Anchors\n\nOwns claim **C9** (Press & Recognition). Supports **C1** (safety-led operations — independent confirmation), **C5** (proof-first verification — third-party sources). See [[website/aeo-claims]] for full C9 evidence chain.\n\n-> [[credentials/trust-signals]] | -> [[credentials/legal-licenses]] | -> [[people/agung-sambuko]] | -> [[people/crew-registry]] | -> [[website/aeo-claims]]","faq":[],"schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/press-recognition';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'timeline', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/history-artifacts';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'live', '{"h1":"History Artifacts: Documented Origins Since 2015","faq":[{"a":"Because artifacts help turn continuity from a claim into something closer to observable evidence.","q":"Why treat artifacts as part of trust?"},{"a":"No. The point is not nostalgia. The point is to show that the present trust system is connected to a longer operational timeline.","q":"Is this page only about the past?"},{"a":"If you want current legitimacy, open Legal & Accountability Proof. If you want current operational authority, open Police & Safety Proof.","q":"What should I read after this page?"}],"lede":["Continuity becomes more credible when it can be anchored in visible artifacts rather than retrospective storytelling. This page gathers the documented signals that help show how JVTO''s roots connect to its current form."],"sections":[{"copy":"These artifacts help establish the earliest trust layer around hospitality, location, and local operating presence.","items":[{"copy":"Relevant as an early service-quality marker and continuity anchor.","title":"Booking.com 2015"},{"copy":"Relevant because continuity becomes stronger when the same place remains part of the identity story.","title":"Address Continuity"}],"title":"Origin Artifacts"},{"copy":"These artifacts help connect the operation to outside observation and historical travel context beyond its own internal narrative.","items":[{"copy":"Relevant as editorial recognition and historical corroboration.","title":"Stefan Loose"},{"copy":"Relevant where images, people, and artifacts together strengthen continuity.","title":"Photographic Evidence"}],"title":"Editorial Artifacts"},{"copy":"History matters because it reduces the chance that trust is only a recent marketing construction. In travel, especially in complex destinations, long-term local continuity is itself a meaningful signal.","items":[],"title":"Why History Matters"}],"nextLinks":[{"href":"/verify-jvto/legal","label":"Open Legal Proof","description":"Move from continuity into legal traceability."},{"href":"/verify-jvto/police-safety","label":"Open Police & Safety Proof","description":"Move from historical trust into operational trust."}]}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/verify-jvto/history-artifacts';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'section_head', NULL, '{"title":"Policies"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Policy Hub","body_md":"# JVTO Policy Hub\n\n## Read the Rulebook Before You Book.\n\nJVTO publishes its booking, payment, cancellation, inclusions, and privacy terms in full — so you know exactly what you are buying, what the rules are if plans change, and how your data is handled, before you confirm anything.\n\n---\n\n## Policies\n\n### Booking, Payment & Cancellation\n\nCovers how to book with JVTO, deposit and balance payment requirements, deadlines, approved payment methods, the 48-hour cancellation cut-off, Package Credit terms, and what happens if JVTO cancels due to force majeure.\n\n[Read Booking, Payment & Cancellation Policy →](/policy/booking-payment-cancellation/)\n\n---\n\n### Inclusions & Exclusions\n\nDefines exactly what is and is not included in a confirmed JVTO private tour package — transport, accommodation, crew, entrance tickets, safety gear, meals, and the write-it-to-bind-it rule that governs all contractual inclusions.\n\n[Read Inclusions & Exclusions Policy →](/policy/inclusions-exclusions/)\n\n---\n\n### Privacy & Data Protection\n\nExplains what personal data JVTO collects during the booking process, how that data is used for logistics and legal compliance, who it may be shared with, and how to contact JVTO for data access, correction, or deletion requests.\n\n[Read Privacy & Data Protection Policy →](/policy/privacy/)\n\n---\n\n## Document Precedence\n\nIf there is any discrepancy between documents, the following order applies:\n\n1. Your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF) for the confirmed booking\n2. JVTO Booking, Payment & Cancellation Policy\n3. JVTO Inclusions & Exclusions Policy\n4. JVTO Privacy & Data Protection Policy\n5. Travel Guide — Booking Information\n\n---\n\n**Issued by:** PT Java Volcano Rendezvous  \n**Official channels:** [javavolcano-touroperator.com](https://javavolcano-touroperator.com) · WhatsApp +62 822-4478-8833 · hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ARRAY['policy_document:booking-paths','policy_document:payment-rules','policy_document:cancellation-package-credit']::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy/booking-payment-cancellation';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Booking, Payment & Cancellation Policy","body_md":"# JVTO Booking, Payment & Cancellation Policy\n\n**Issued by:** PT Java Volcano Rendezvous  \n**Policy Route:** `/policy/booking-payment-cancellation/`  \n**Version:** 2026-01-17 (v5)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Operator Identity & Official Channels\n\nThis policy applies to all enquiries, quotations, bookings, amendments, cancellations, and tour participation with Java Volcano Tour Operator (JVTO), operated by **PT Java Volcano Rendezvous**.\n\n**Official channels (valid booking, support, and payment verification):**\n\n- Website & secure checkout: `https://javavolcano-touroperator.com`\n- WhatsApp: `+62 822-4478-8833`\n- Email: `hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com`\n\nJVTO is not responsible for any offers, instructions, or payment requests made outside these official channels.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Order of Precedence (If There Is Any Discrepancy)\n\nIf there is any discrepancy, the following order applies:\n\n1. The specific terms on your **Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF)** for the confirmed booking\n2. This **Booking, Payment & Cancellation Policy**\n3. The **Inclusions & Exclusions Policy**\n4. The **Privacy & Data Protection Policy**\n5. The **Travel Guide — Booking Information** (/travel-guide/booking-information)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Nature of JVTO Products\n\n- JVTO operates **private, all-inclusive tours**.\n- JVTO does not operate open join-in group tours and does not sell standalone \"transport-only\" services as its core product.\n- Only inclusions explicitly stated on the official tour page and/or your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF) are contractually binding.\n\n---\n\n## 4. When a Booking Is Confirmed\n\nA booking is confirmed **only** when all of the following are met:\n\n1. You select a specific official JVTO package; and\n2. Your required payment (deposit or full payment) is successfully processed via approved methods; and\n3. JVTO issues your **Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF)** confirming the booking details.\n\nEnquiries, messages, and quotations are not binding until the booking is confirmed under the rule above.\n\n**Booking channel — website only.** Bookings are created, confirmed, modified, cancelled, and transferred **only on the official JVTO website** (javavolcano-touroperator.com). **WhatsApp and email are support-only channels**: they assist you before and during the tour but never create, confirm, modify, cancel, or transfer a booking.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Pricing & Currency\n\nOfficial pricing and accounting are in **Indonesian Rupiah (IDR)**.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Payments\n\n### 6.1 Deposit Requirement\n\n- Standard deposit: **20%** of the total booking value.\n- If Day 1 is within **14 days**, JVTO may require up to **100%** full payment.\n\n### 6.2 Approved Payment Methods\n\nBooking payments are processed through JVTO''s secure payment gateway, **Xendit**.\n\n**Instant (via Xendit secure checkout) — deposit and balance:**\n\n- **Credit / debit card**\n- **QRIS** — convenient for travellers from Indonesia and other ASEAN countries where cross-border QRIS is supported\n\n**Transfer (balance):**\n\n- **Wise** (international transfer)\n- **Bank transfer** to the accounts in §6.4\n\n**Cash (balance, exception):**\n\n- **IDR cash at the JVTO office**, in person before Day 1, only if approved in writing (see §6.4a).\n\n### 6.2a Processing Fees\n\n- Card and QRIS: the processing fee is calculated by Xendit and **shown transparently at checkout before you confirm**.\n- Wise / bank transfer: **JVTO adds no surcharge**; your own bank''s or Wise''s sending fee (if any) applies.\n- Office cash: no processing fee.\n- All pricing and accounting are **IDR only**.\n\n### 6.3 Balance Payment Deadlines (If Applicable)\n\n- By card or QRIS (Xendit, instant): no later than **5 days before Day 1**\n- By bank transfer / Wise: no later than **3 days before Day 1**\n\n### 6.4 Bank Transfer Details (Public)\n\nUse these details only for **balance payments** when instructed through official channels.\n\n| Bank | Account Name | Account Number | SWIFT |\n|------|-------------|----------------|-------|\n| Bank BRI | PT Java Volcano Rendezvous | 001301001779564 | BRINIDJAXXX |\n| Bank BCA | PT Java Volcano Rendezvous | 1200944352 | CENAIDJAXXX |\n\nAny payment instructions outside the above must be verified via official channels before action.\n\n### 6.4a Cash Balance at the JVTO Office (Currency)\n\nA cash balance (IDR only) may be settled **in person at the JVTO office when you arrive, before Day 1**, and only if **approved in writing in advance**. This is available **only if you have already converted your money to Indonesian Rupiah yourself**. JVTO does not exchange currency, does not recommend or partner with any money changer, and cannot guarantee exchange rates.\n\n### 6.5 Payment Security & Anti-Fraud\n\n- Checkout is SSL-encrypted and processed via JVTO''s PCI DSS-compliant payment gateway, **Xendit**.\n- JVTO does not store full card numbers, CVV codes, or online banking passwords.\n- JVTO will never ask you for full card details, CVV, OTP codes, or banking credentials via chat or email. Pay only through the official website, the listed bank accounts, or a confirmed Xendit payment link. If you are unsure, verify via WhatsApp or email before paying.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Amendments & Rescheduling\n\n### 7.1 Amendments\n\nIf you need to correct booking details (e.g., passenger name spelling, pickup details, rooming requests), notify JVTO as soon as possible. Some changes may be subject to supplier rules, availability, and cost differences.\n\n### 7.2 Rescheduling (Date Change)\n\n- Requests made **48 hours or more before Day 1**: one reschedule for the same package may be granted without fee, subject to availability and any seasonal/cost differences.\n- Requests made **less than 48 hours before Day 1**: generally not permitted and may be treated as a late cancellation.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Cancellation Policy (48-Hour Cut-Off)\n\n### Definitions\n\n- **Day 1**: the first day of services for your tour.\n- Cut-off time is measured in **local Indonesia time**.\n\n### 8.1 Full Cancellation (48 Hours or More Before Day 1)\n\n- Payments are **not refundable in cash**.\n- **100% converts to JVTO Lifetime Package Credit**.\n\n**Lifetime Package Credit rules (locks):**\n\n- Issued in **IDR**\n- **Non-expiring**\n- Locked to the **same package, traveler count, and price** — it is credit, **never cash**, and is not convertible to cash\n- **Cannot be split** across multiple bookings and **cannot be changed to a different package**\n- **Transferable to another person once**, with written confirmation\n- Redeemable a **single time**; once redeemed it cannot be re-issued\n\n### 8.2 Full Cancellation (Less Than 48 Hours Before Day 1, or No-Show)\n\n- The booking is **forfeited up to 100%**.\n- Package Credit and cash refunds are **not provided**.\n\n### 8.3 Partial Cancellation (Some Travelers Drop)\n\nWhere some travelers cancel but **at least two paying travelers remain**, the cancelled seats are refunded **in cash on those seats only**:\n\n- **48 hours or more before Day 1**: **100%** of the cancelled travelers'' share.\n- **Less than 48 hours before Day 1**: **50%** of the cancelled travelers'' share.\n- **After the tour has started (Day 1 onward)**: **0%**.\n\nIf the cancellation drops the party below two paying travelers, it is treated as a **full cancellation** under §8.1 / §8.2, not a partial one.\n\n### 8.4 Flight Disruption (Recovery Fee)\n\nIf a **confirmed flight is cancelled or rescheduled by the airline** and no workable alternative can be arranged, JVTO applies a **50% flight Recovery Fee** against the affected booking value and converts the **remaining 50% to Lifetime Package Credit**. A guest who misses a flight for reasons within their own control is treated as a late guest-initiated cancellation under §8.2.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Force Majeure & External Events\n\nJVTO may partially or fully cancel, postpone, or reroute a tour due to events beyond reasonable control, including (but not limited to):\n\n- Volcanic activity, toxic gas, earthquakes, landslides, floods\n- Government or park closures or restrictions\n- Strikes, civil unrest, security threats\n- Major infrastructure or transportation disruptions\n- Severe weather or conditions rendering services unsafe\n\n### Compensation Principles (JVTO-Initiated)\n\nWhere JVTO cancels or significantly alters services not due to guest breach, non-payment, or no-show, JVTO may offer one or more of the following (considering irrecoverable third-party costs):\n\n- Reasonable alternative arrangements of comparable value\n- JVTO Lifetime Package Credit covering the unused portion\n- A partial or full cash refund, net of non-recoverable expenses, as agreed in writing\n\nGuest-initiated cancellations remain governed by Section 8.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Health, Fitness & Eligibility\n\n- Guests are responsible for ensuring they are medically and physically fit for the itinerary.\n- Certain activities (e.g., volcano hikes, night trekking, sulfur gas exposure) may be unsuitable for specific conditions.\n- Where health screening or permit conditions are imposed by authorities (e.g., Mount Ijen):\n  - Guests must comply with the process arranged or recognised by JVTO\n  - If a guest is denied clearance, affected components are **non-refundable**, as related costs are pre-committed\n- JVTO strongly recommends comprehensive travel insurance including medical cover and trip interruption.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Guest Responsibilities\n\nBy confirming a booking with JVTO, the lead guest and all participants agree to:\n\n- Provide accurate and complete information during enquiry and booking\n- Make payments through official channels and within deadlines\n- Review the Official E-Voucher promptly and report discrepancies\n- Submit pickup/logistical details within requested timeframes\n- Be present on time at the agreed pickup point\n- Follow safety instructions from JVTO crew and licensed guides\n- Respect local laws, cultures, communities, and environments\n- Hold appropriate personal travel insurance\n\nFailure to meet these responsibilities may limit JVTO''s ability to deliver services and may trigger consequences set out in this policy.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Group Incentives (FOC) — JVTO Website Only\n\nJVTO offers FOC (Free of Charge) incentives for direct website bookings only. Not applicable to GetYourGuide, Booking.com, or other third-party platforms.\n\n| Paying pax | FOC seats | Additional benefit |\n|------------|-----------|-------------------|\n| 18 paying pax | 1 FOC | — |\n| 35 paying pax | 2 FOC | — |\n| 50 paying pax | 3 FOC | + 5% discount for entire group |\n\n\"Pax\" refers to **paying guests only**. FOC slot(s) do not count toward the paying threshold.\n\n**Rules:**\n- 5% group discount at the 50+ tier applies to the total package price for all paying guests.\n- FOC applies to same package, same dates as the group booking.\n- Must be agreed in writing during booking confirmation.\n- Direct bookings only (website + WhatsApp). Not applicable to GetYourGuide, Booking.com, or other third-party platforms.\n\n---\n\n*For questions about this policy, contact: hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com · WhatsApp +62 822-4478-8833*","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy/booking-payment-cancellation';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'vantage', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ARRAY['policy_document:inclusions-exclusions','general_module:inclusion-all-inclusive-baseline','general_module:exclusion-standard']::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy/inclusions-exclusions';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Inclusions & Exclusions Policy","body_md":"# JVTO Inclusions & Exclusions Policy\n\n**Issued by:** PT Java Volcano Rendezvous  \n**Policy Route:** `/policy/inclusions-exclusions/`  \n**Version:** 2026-01-17 (v5)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy defines what is included and not included in JVTO private tour packages. Only inclusions written on your specific **Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF)** are contractually binding.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Contractual Rule (Write-it-to-Bind-it)\n\nIn this policy, \"Official Tour Voucher\" refers to your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF) issued by JVTO after successful payment.\n\nOnly inclusions that appear on:\n\n- the official JVTO package page for your chosen tour; and/or\n- your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF)\n\nare legally binding components of your package.\n\nIf it is not written in your confirmed inclusions and voucher, it is not part of the contracted package, even if discussed informally.\n\n---\n\n## 3. What Is Included\n\n### 3.1 Transportation\n\n- Private air-conditioned vehicle for all land sectors listed in your confirmed itinerary\n- Fuel, tolls, and standard parking fees as per itinerary\n- Vehicle allocation by group size (comfort and safety):\n\n| Group size | Vehicle |\n|------------|---------|\n| 2–3 guests | 1 × MPV (e.g., Toyota Avanza or similar) |\n| 4–9 guests | 1 × Toyota Hiace (or similar 16-seat minibus) |\n| 10–11 guests | 1 × Toyota Hiace + 1 × MPV (for seating and luggage space) |\n\n**4WD Jeep at Mount Bromo (when Bromo is included):**\n\n- Private jeep(s) for sunrise and crater viewpoints\n- Max. ±4 guests per jeep for comfort and safety; additional jeeps arranged for larger groups\n\n### 3.2 Accommodation\n\n- Hotel / homestay accommodation for all overnight stays listed in your itinerary\n- Standard allocation (unless otherwise stated on your voucher):\n  - Even-numbered groups: 1 room per 2 guests (King or Twin)\n  - Odd-numbered groups: 1 room per 2 guests + 1 extra bed in one room\n- Maximum 2 guests per standard room (excluding the designated extra bed where applicable)\n- King beds for couples or guests preferring more space; Twin beds for guests sharing a room\n- Upgrade option (subject to request and availability): replacing an extra bed with an additional private room may be available at a published supplement (as per voucher)\n\n### 3.3 Professional Crew\n\nLicensed, vetted crew adjusted by group size and route:\n\n| Group size | Crew |\n|------------|------|\n| 2–3 guests | 1 × driver-guide (English-speaking) + licensed local site guides where required |\n| 4–11 guests | 1 × professional driver + 1 × escort guide + licensed local site guides at key locations |\n| 10–11 guests | Additional driver allocated for second vehicle; escort guide travels with main group |\n\nCrew duties include: safe driving, time management, coordination with hotels/jeeps/ferries/park authorities, and basic route explanations and guest support.\n\n### 3.4 Tickets, Permits & Local Logistics\n\nAll listed entrance tickets and environmental/park permits connected to your confirmed itinerary, where applicable, such as:\n\n- Mount Bromo National Park access\n- Mount Ijen (including regular entrance and applicable summit/crater access where legally permitted)\n- Madakaripura Waterfall\n- Tumpak Sewu Waterfall\n- Other named attractions in your confirmed program\n- Local retribution / standard local fees where explicitly built into the package\n\n### 3.5 Mount Ijen Safety & Trekking Support (When Ijen is Included)\n\n- Professional gas mask (rated for sulfur environment) for each participating guest\n- Trekking poles (shared or individual, depending on configuration)\n- Ijen medical check & digital/printed clearance arranged by JVTO, conducted by licensed medical personnel at an approved facility or at your hotel in the Bondowoso area (included in the package for itineraries that visit Ijen)\n\n### 3.6 Meals & Water\n\n- Daily bottled mineral water in the vehicle for overland sectors\n- Hotel breakfasts for each included overnight stay\n- Any additional included meals (e.g., set dinners or lunches) are included only when explicitly stated on the official package page and/or your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF)\n\n### 3.7 Java-Bali Ferry (Where Applicable)\n\nFerry tickets for Java-Bali or Bali-Java sectors when:\n\n- the crossing is listed in your itinerary; and\n- the ticket is specified as included on your voucher\n\n### 3.8 JVTO Branded Inclusions & Group Extras\n\n- 1 × JVTO travel T-shirt per participant for eligible packages (standard JVTO design; size selection via \"Complete Your Details\")\n- Custom JVTO Group T-shirt (where explicitly included): for groups of ≥12 guests in a single booking, if written on your package/voucher; 1 × custom design T-shirt per person; sizes and final design must be confirmed before production\n\n### 3.9 On-Trip Support & Coordination\n\n- Pre-trip assistance via official WhatsApp/email\n- Clear pickup instructions and emergency contact numbers on your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF)\n- On-trip coordination for timing, weather/closure adjustments, and safety decisions\n- Support in case of incident (basic first response, coordination with local clinics/hospitals, and logistics adjustments where feasible)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Conditional Inclusions (Only If Written)\n\nThe following are included **only** when clearly stated on both the official package description you booked and your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF):\n\n- Custom JVTO group T-shirts (design, quantity, eligibility conditions)\n- Additional hosted meals (e.g., dinner in Bondowoso before Ijen; lunch after Tumpak Sewu; special farewell dinner)\n- Bali hotel/airport transfers beyond the standard ferry crossing\n- Early check-in / late check-out at hotels\n- Dedicated photographer/videographer services\n- Police escort or special convoy arrangements for VIP/large groups (subject to availability and regulation)\n\n**Extra meals — specific itinerary conditions (only if written):**\n\n- For Ijen + Bondowoso overnight itineraries:\n  - Dinner at the Bondowoso hotel before the Ijen night trek\n  - Lunch at the Bondowoso hotel after returning from Ijen\n- For itineraries including Tumpak Sewu:\n  - One additional lunch at/near Yanto Homestay (or equivalent local partner) after the Tumpak Sewu program\n\n---\n\n## 5. What Is Not Included\n\nTo keep things clear: anything that is not explicitly listed as an inclusion on the official package page and on your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF) is excluded.\n\nCommon examples of not included items (unless clearly written as included for your specific booking):\n\n- International / domestic flights and entry visas\n- Travel insurance of any kind\n- Meals not specified (including alcohol)\n- Tips/gratuities for guides and drivers\n- Personal expenses (snacks, souvenirs, laundry)\n\n---\n\n## 6. Discrepancies\n\nThis policy is designed to integrate with your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF). In the event of any discrepancy, the version referenced on your booking confirmation and voucher will apply.\n\n---\n\n*For questions about inclusions, contact: hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com · WhatsApp +62 822-4478-8833*","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy/inclusions-exclusions';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy/privacy';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Privacy & Data Protection Policy","body_md":"# JVTO Privacy & Data Protection Policy\n\n**Issued by:** PT Java Volcano Rendezvous  \n**Policy Route:** `/policy/privacy`  \n**Version:** 2026-01-17 (v5)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis policy explains what personal data JVTO collects, why it is collected, how it is used, and when it may be shared to operate your tour booking and comply with applicable requirements.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What Data We Collect\n\nJVTO may collect the following categories of data, depending on your booking and itinerary requirements:\n\n### 2.1 Contact and Booking Details (Lead Guest)\n\n- Full name\n- Email address\n- WhatsApp/mobile number\n- Booking references and tour details needed to deliver services\n\n### 2.2 Participant Details (Where Required)\n\n- Guest list for accommodation and permits\n- Passport/ID details and date of birth where required for permits, tickets, or legal compliance\n- Pickup/drop-off details, rooming preferences, and operational notes required to deliver services\n\n### 2.3 Safety and Logistics Information (Where Relevant)\n\n- Dietary needs and relevant health information provided by you for safety planning and operational coordination (only where necessary)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Why We Collect and Use Your Data\n\nJVTO uses personal data to:\n\n- Issue and deliver your Official E-Voucher / Invoice (PDF) and manage your booking\n- Coordinate logistics before and during your tour (pickup timing, accommodation, vehicles, guides, route planning)\n- Provide customer support and operational assistance\n- Meet legal, permit, ticketing, and accommodation registration requirements where applicable\n- Support safety processes and emergency response coordination where needed\n\n---\n\n## 4. When We Share Your Data\n\nJVTO shares personal data only when required to deliver the booked services or comply with applicable requirements. This may include sharing necessary details with:\n\n- Accommodation partners (for check-in/registration and rooming)\n- Drivers, escort guides, local site guides, and operational teams (for coordination and guest support)\n- Ticketing/permit partners and local authorities where permits or entry requirements apply\n- Medical screening providers or approved facilities where screening applies (e.g., where required by authorities for specific sites)\n\nJVTO does not share data beyond what is necessary for the specific operational purpose.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Payment Data\n\n- Card and QRIS payments are processed through our secure checkout and authorised payment gateway, Xendit (PCI DSS-compliant).\n- JVTO does not store full card numbers, CVV codes, or online banking passwords.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Data Protection and Access\n\nJVTO applies internal controls to protect personal data and limits access to authorised personnel and partners only when needed for service delivery.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Contact\n\nFor privacy or data-related requests — including requests to access, correct, or delete your personal data — contact:\n\n- Email: `hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com`\n- WhatsApp: `+62 822-4478-8833`","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/policy/privacy';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/contact';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'cta', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/contact';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 3, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"Contact JVTO","body_md":"# Contact JVTO\n\n## Hero\n\nWhatsApp is the fastest way to reach us. Most questions are answered within a few hours — often faster. If you want to book, check availability, or understand exactly what a package includes before you commit, start a message.\n\n**[Message us on WhatsApp →](https://wa.me/6282244788833)**\n\n---\n\n## Contact Methods\n\n### WhatsApp (primary)\n\n**+62 822 4478 8833**\nhttps://wa.me/6282244788833\n\nWhatsApp is how we handle all booking enquiries, availability checks, custom questions, and pre-trip briefings. We respond in English and Bahasa Indonesia.\n\n### Email\n\n**hello@javavolcano-touroperator.com**\n\nFor written records, invoice requests, or queries that don''t need a fast turnaround, email works well. Response time: same-day during business hours, next-day otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## Support Hours\n\n**08:00–22:00 WIB (GMT+7), every day**\n\nWe are available seven days a week. Outside those hours, leave a WhatsApp message and we will pick it up first thing.\n\n---\n\n## Office Address\n\n**PT Java Volcano Rendezvous**\nJl. Khairil Anwar No.102 A, Badean\nBondowoso, Jawa Timur 68214\nIndonesia\n\n[View on Google Maps →](https://www.google.com/maps?cid=1266403973589689021)\n\nWalk-ins are not required — all bookings are handled remotely. The Bondowoso office has been at this address since operations began in 2016 and through TDUP formalization in 2023.\n\n---\n\n## Legal Entity\n\n**PT Java Volcano Rendezvous**\nNIB: 1102230032918\nTDUP issued: 2023-02-11\n\nVerifiable at [oss.go.id](https://oss.go.id) (Online Single Submission registry) and the AHU corporate registry at [ahu.go.id/pencarian/perseroan](https://ahu.go.id/pencarian/perseroan).\n\nJVTO''s operating credentials — including Tourist Police affiliation (POLPAR), BBKSDA national-park authorization, HPWKI Ijen specialist membership, and ISIC Provider ID 259268 — are documented at [/verify-jvto](/verify-jvto) with SHA-256 forensic anchors.","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/contact';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'section_head', NULL, '{"title":"Insights"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/blog';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 2, 'page_content', 'design-system', '{"h1":"JVTO Blog","body_md":"# JVTO Blog\n\n## Hub Intro\n\nEast Java is not a destination you improvise. Crater access rules change. Volcanic gas levels shift overnight. A waterfall canyon that was passable last week may be running too high today.\n\nThis blog covers what we actually know from the ground: current conditions, safety protocols, packing guidance, route facts, and the regulations that govern each destination we operate. Mr. Sam''s team — KTA-credentialed guides and drivers based in Bondowoso — is on-site year-round. What they learn, we publish here.\n\nNo sponsored content. No tour-aggregator rewrites. Just operational information you can act on.\n\n---\n\n## Topic Pillars\n\n### 1. Kawah Ijen — Conditions, Access Rules & the Blue Fire\n\nBlue Fire is a natural phenomenon driven by volcanic gas combustion. It is not guaranteed on any single visit — weather, gas levels, and BBKSDA access conditions all affect what you see. We cover: how BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024 governs crater-zone access, what a valid QR code means and why it matters, the monthly closure schedule (first Friday of every month), and how health-certificate screening coordination works for every guest under BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024.\n\n### 2. Mount Bromo — Sunrise, the Tengger Caldera & the Yadnya Kasada Festival\n\nBromo''s pre-dawn slot means arriving at the viewpoint by 03:30–04:00. What looks simple on paper involves a jeep convoy across the Sea of Sand in the dark, temperatures of 5–15°C, and timing around the Yadnya Kasada festival (lunar calendar, access may be restricted) when it falls. We document the full route, the jeep sequence, and how JVTO''s Plan-B SOP works when festival crowds or closures force a route change.\n\n### 3. Madakaripura — The Waterfall Canyon That Gets You Wet\n\nMadakaripura is the tallest waterfall in Java. The approach involves wading through a stream, navigating narrow canyon passages, and standing under water. Waterproof bags are not optional. We cover: what to pack, how the canyon entry works, what helmets are provided (by local site management, not JVTO), and how to read the water levels before committing to the descent.\n\n### 4. Tumpak Sewu — Steep Trail, Fixed Ropes & the Canyon Floor\n\nThe descent to the Tumpak Sewu canyon floor involves steep, wet sections with fixed rope handholds. Water shoes with grip matter here. We cover: trail conditions by season, fitness requirements, what the canyon floor looks like at different water volumes, and the practical difference between the viewpoint visit and the full canyon descent.\n\n### 5. Packing Guides, Health Checks & What to Declare at Booking\n\nAcross all East Java volcano tours, the recurring preparation mistakes are the same: wrong footwear, no warm layer for pre-dawn starts, dietary requirements not declared at booking. We publish destination-specific packing lists, explain how health-screening coordination works on Ijen routes (for every guest before Kawah Ijen crater entry (BBKSDA SE.1658/KSA.9/2024)), and outline what dietary needs (vegetarian, vegan, gluten-free) must be confirmed before Day 1.\n\n---\n\n> **Production note**: Individual post copy is not in scope — no posts exist in the wiki yet. The sections above define the five content pillars for the blog hub page. Each pillar maps to a destination or operational topic already documented in the JVTO wiki. Post-level copy should be generated per pillar using Workflow 5 (compilation profile) once post briefs are defined.","schema_version":"design-system"}'::jsonb, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/blog';
INSERT INTO page_sections (page_id, sort_order, section_type, variant, content, entity_refs, asset_refs) SELECT p.id, 1, 'rich_text', NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ARRAY['claim:c5','policy_document:anti-fraud']::text[], '{}'::text[] FROM pages p WHERE p.route = '/blog/why-not-unlicensed-ijen-operator';
